1
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,577
Kirito, he finally woke up!

2
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:15,880
Kirito, you're back.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,197
About damn time you snapped out of it.

4
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:26,104
I knew if I waited around long
enough you wouldn't disappoint me.

5
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,420
We didn't get to finish
things back in Aincrad.

6
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:43,960
Now, I can check that off my list.

7
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,260
It's showtime, baby.

8
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:10,540
I don't know.

9
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:34,430
Thank you

10
00:01:34,513 --> 00:01:41,500
so

11
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:59,140
much for watching.

12
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:40,880
Is that all you've got?

13
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:43,747
I want to fight, so get
the lead out already!

14
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:49,920
Come on, man!

15
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:52,965
I've been waiting damn
near two years for this!

16
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:07,497
You'd kill me faster if you dropped that
broken-ass sword and used both hands.

17
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:09,737
Then you could go after all these others

18
00:03:09,820 --> 00:03:12,277
that were killing your
friends a minute ago.

19
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:15,007
They only did that
because you made them two.

20
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:16,691
That's how you do things,

21
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:20,377
turning people against each other
and watching all hell break loose.

22
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:22,700
That's what you did with us in SAO.

23
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:24,737
Oh, that ain't gonna happen here.

24
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:25,840
Never again.

25
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:27,660
I'll make sure of that.

26
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,740
Oh, it'll happen again.

27
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:32,677
Once those players thaw out,

28
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:36,017
they'll go right back to
slaughtering all of your friends.

29
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:38,300
Unless your pals kill them first.

30
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:41,937
There's no honor in killing the
Helpless, but that's the point.

31
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:43,300
So give the order.

32
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,300
Kill all the red players!

33
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:50,617
Hey, if you want to be
stubborn, that's cool with me.

34
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,171
I'll kill you either way.

35
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,260
But after I get done with you,

36
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:57,385
I'm gonna put Lightning Flash,

37
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:01,300
your whole crew, and every single
Underworld are into coffins.

38
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:02,834
You can count on that!

39
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:09,470
Kirito!

40
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:15,840
Eugeo, please help him.

41
00:04:31,660 --> 00:04:33,520
What the hell?

42
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:47,200
Let's go. You and me. Chiyo.

43
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:17,840
Release recollection!

44
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:30,700
Now what?

45
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:46,600
It's the life resources
of the foreign players.

46
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:51,877
Kirito logged them out without making
them suffer the pain of getting killed.

47
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:54,431
You're going to pay for that, you bastard!

48
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:57,060
Oh no! Stop him!

49
00:05:57,380 --> 00:05:58,320
Don't worry.

50
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:01,470
Look it!

51
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:04,470
Damn it!

52
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:05,980
What's going on?

53
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,826
Why aren't they coming to me?

54
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:09,620
Lives are like vessels.

55
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:13,300
They carry our hopes and
dreams and reflect our souls.

56
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:16,077
Do you think all these players
from different countries

57
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:19,454
came here just so they could
be used to kill each other?

58
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:23,234
Nah, they want to have fun
and explore a cool new world.

59
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:26,973
A place that's totally different
from anything they know.

60
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:30,458
A place like the land of
fairies where you and I met.

61
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,820
They want the same as us.

62
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:37,680
You're right, Yuki.

63
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:50,800
Release. Recollection.

64
00:06:58,140 --> 00:06:59,840
Son of a bitch!

65
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:06,717
Eugeo once told me that in the
northernmost part of the human empire,

66
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:11,580
There was an enormous black cedar tree
and Kirito sword was forged from it.

67
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:15,460
I see that explains why
it can absorb sacred power

68
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:52,560
Man, Kirito, you really are the best.

69
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:55,817
No one from back in
the Aincrad days to now

70
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:58,782
ever brought out the killer
in me as much as you.

71
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:01,777
Sex like hell, it's gotta
end after all that time,

72
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:05,036
but there's no better place
to end it than right here.

73
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:09,104
Let's you and me have
some fun, Black Swordsman.

74
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:11,766
Okay, I'm ready when you are.

75
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,080
First element!

76
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:32,540
Oh, my God.

77
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:47,960
No!

78
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:02,940
Now that's what I'm talking about.

79
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:06,240
But you didn't get rid of me.

80
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,310
Oh, no.

81
00:10:07,393 --> 00:10:09,160
You just logged me out is all.

82
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:12,460
I'm still gonna keep
coming after you guys.

83
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:17,157
And I won't stop till I
slit you and Lightning

84
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:20,820
Flash's throats and
ripped out your hearts.

85
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:24,160
You can both count on that. Uh-uh.

86
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,760
You're done for good.

87
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:32,799
You'll never log out of here again.

88
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:34,180
Count on that.

89
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:47,840
My sword's made from the Giga Cedar.

90
00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:51,660
A huge tree in Rulid they
couldn't cut down for 200 years.

91
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,580
Till two kids finally did.

92
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,380
I just sent the memory of it into you.

93
00:10:56,680 --> 00:11:00,537
When your friends see all those players
logging out, they'll speed up time,

94
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:02,240
trapping you in your STL.

95
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:06,116
It'll be years before you're
let out, if you're lucky.

96
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:10,437
Then again, folks might want
to build a village here.

97
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:14,991
They'll need wood and who knows, maybe
a couple kids will chop you down too.

98
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:26,540
System call, transfer
durability, right to area.

99
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:55,080
Kitty-toe, you did it again, man.

100
00:11:56,380 --> 00:12:00,820
You saved everyone here, but you've
got to stop hogging all the glory,

101
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:02,924
dude, because it's getting old.

102
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:11,940
That cat's off the hook, for real.

103
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:13,300
He did it!

104
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:15,840
Thank God he did it! He did!

105
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:17,420
And I'm so happy!

106
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:35,818
Ever since I first laid eyes on him,

107
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:41,260
I had faith in him, that at the last moment,
he and those swords would save us all.

108
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:48,077
Thank you, everyone.

109
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:53,100
I won't let your faith in me, or all the
blood and tears you shed, be for nothing.

110
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,700
I mean it. Thank you.

111
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:08,620
Kirito, Emperor Vecta,
he's after... I know.

112
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:11,300
It's fuzzy, but I know he's after Alice.

113
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,200
Let's go get her back.

114
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:14,680
You and me, Asuna.

115
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:35,200
Come on.

116
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:37,600
Wait, Kitty-Do, what are you doing?

117
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:39,020
Hold on tight.

118
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,270
Damn it!

119
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:57,855
What's that idiot standing around for?

120
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:06,820
We got a little under 8 hours and 20
minutes to go before the JSDF boards us.

121
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:10,317
Boss wanted me to crank up the
time again at the 8 hour mark,

122
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:12,777
but since the other players got wiped out,

123
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:14,272
might as well do it now.

124
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:18,051
Whatever you're up to in there,
Vassago, you better hang on.

125
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:23,230
What?

126
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:26,860
That figures. I need a key.

127
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:30,160
We're good at picking locks.

128
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:36,020
Higa! Hey! Can you hear
me? Come on! Wake up!

129
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:43,140
How's Kirito?

130
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,558
He's out of danger.

131
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:47,277
His Fluctlight activity's
been fully restored.

132
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:49,654
It's a little too active, to be honest.

133
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:51,050
Really?

134
00:14:51,133 --> 00:14:52,660
Oh, that's good to hear.

135
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:54,000
I swear, Higa.

136
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:56,377
You had me scared for a second there.

137
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:57,320
I'm sorry.

138
00:14:57,580 --> 00:14:59,937
It's all my fault that mole got on board.

139
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:01,897
I should have vetted the staff better.

140
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:03,180
It's okay, Geeks.

141
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:05,397
What about Alice in the Underworld?

142
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:07,009
They're both safe for now.

143
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:11,400
All the players from the US, China,
and South Korea have logged out.

144
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:12,910
Wait.

145
00:15:12,993 --> 00:15:14,260
China and South Korea?

146
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:16,877
They had people logged in from there, too?

147
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:18,120
Yeah, tons of them.

148
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:20,460
They posted all over social media,

149
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:24,777
using their competitiveness as gamers
to rile them up and lure them in.

150
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:25,690
Uh-huh.

151
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:27,060
That would do it.

152
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:30,815
The 2,000 from Japan you
logged in put up a good fight,

153
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:32,697
but they were mostly wiped out.

154
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:37,337
At that point, there were still over 20,000
Chinese and South Korean players left.

155
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:40,832
Luckily, that's when Kirito
woke up, and just like that...

156
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:42,820
Oh, my God.

157
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:47,800
That's not good.

158
00:15:49,540 --> 00:15:52,860
Flutlight Acceleration Rate
Safety Limiter disengaged.

159
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:56,240
15 minutes until maximum
acceleration phase.

160
00:15:56,920 --> 00:16:01,840
For personnel in the STLs, initiate
disengagement protocol immediately. Crap!

161
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:03,820
Maximum acceleration phase?

162
00:16:04,020 --> 00:16:07,480
Isn't the FLA rate limited
to 1,200 times normal speed?

163
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:09,100
Only for folks diving.

164
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:13,067
1,200's the limit for the lifespan
of a real-world human soul.

165
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:17,580
But for observing, we can't speed
it up more than 5,000 times normal.

166
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:20,720
That said, the hardware
can go even faster.

167
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:22,640
But how fast?

168
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:24,697
The hardware does have
a limit, doesn't it?

169
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:30,080
During the maximum acceleration phase, the
FLA rate will be just over five million.

170
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:35,037
The two STLs in Roppongi can't keep up at
that speed, because they're on a sad link.

171
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:37,177
They'll be disconnected automatically.

172
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:40,240
But Kirito's and Asuna's
STLs are hardwired.

173
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:42,160
They're in danger! Come on!

174
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:45,777
We have to get them out of those
STLs right now, but— No, we can't!

175
00:16:45,860 --> 00:16:48,397
The initial acceleration
phase already started.

176
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:51,957
If we pull them out of those machines
now, it'll damage their Fluct Lights!

177
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:53,717
What about the disengagement protocol?

178
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:54,859
Can we start that?

179
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,430
Hey, Keeks.

180
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:59,097
I'm going back to the
maintenance connector.

181
00:16:59,180 --> 00:17:00,010
Understood.

182
00:17:00,093 --> 00:17:01,377
But I'm going to go with you.

183
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:04,817
I think I should be strong enough to
carry you down that ladder on my back.

184
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:05,782
It's too risky.

185
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:08,020
Please, sir, let me take him. No.

186
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:11,558
I need you and the other
agents to defend the stairs.

187
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,637
We have to open the bulkhead again,

188
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:16,157
which means you'll have to
engage the enemy directly.

189
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:18,593
Which means the risk is greater for you.

190
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:21,329
I'm sorry, but that's
the way it has to be.

191
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:23,740
Sir. Yes, sir.

192
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:28,540
Wait a sec!

193
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:31,096
When I was operating the STLs before,

194
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:34,237
I set us up with an open
channel to talk to Kirito.

195
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:35,800
He's on line C12.

196
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,497
Hurry up and call him now!

197
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:38,698
What do I tell him?

198
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:40,447
Tell him to log himself out!

199
00:17:42,620 --> 00:17:45,100
Is Alice safe? Can you tell?

200
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:49,536
She hasn't been caught yet, but
there's a massive presence chasing her.

201
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,030
Oh boy.

202
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:54,120
I hope we can catch up to
her before it's too late.

203
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:58,257
Kirito, can you hear me?

204
00:17:58,340 --> 00:18:00,340
Kirito, come in! Kikuoka?

205
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,240
How am I hearing you?

206
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:03,860
I'm not at a console.

207
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:06,077
Never mind that, just listen.

208
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,637
You're in a lot of danger.

209
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:09,357
The time acceleration rate is increasing

210
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:12,322
because the hijackers
disengaged the FLA limiter.

211
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:13,490
The limiter?

212
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:17,437
Higa says if you're still in there
when we reach maximum acceleration,

213
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:22,060
by the time we disconnect you here,
200 years will have passed there. What?

214
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:27,757
You and Asuna have ten minutes to
reach the console and log out manually.

215
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:31,134
Depleting your HP is another
option, but it's too risky.

216
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:33,737
If you die after we reach
maximum acceleration,

217
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:38,257
you'll spend 200 years in the Underworld
in a state of total sensory deprivation.

218
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:39,170
Got it.

219
00:18:39,253 --> 00:18:41,997
Me and Asuna are headed for the
console at the World's End Altar.

220
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:44,537
I'll catch up to Alice
in a bit, so get ready.

221
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:46,032
We're bringing her, too.

222
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:49,417
Thanks, but you two are more important.

223
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:53,120
I want you to prioritize your
escape over securing Alice.

224
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:57,137
Two hundred years is longer than
the lifespan of a human soul.

225
00:18:57,220 --> 00:19:00,537
So even though we can delete your
memories after logging you out,

226
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:02,297
if you've been in there that long,

227
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:06,262
the odds of you regaining consciousness
here would be almost zero.

228
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:08,668
Don't worry, we'll make it.

229
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:09,920
We'll all make it.

230
00:19:10,220 --> 00:19:11,660
Oh, and one more thing.

231
00:19:12,720 --> 00:19:15,917
I'm sorry, you know, for
calling you a son of a bitch.

232
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,140
Not at all.

233
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:20,616
I deserved it, and you can
punch me when you get back.

234
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:22,957
It looks like he gets ready.

235
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:24,880
I have to go. Good luck.

236
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:26,410
You too.

237
00:19:26,493 --> 00:19:27,989
We'll get to that console.

238
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:29,062
See you in ten.

239
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:31,660
What did he say?

240
00:19:32,060 --> 00:19:34,460
You sounded like it was serious. Is it?

241
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:36,880
Well, is it? Not really.

242
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:39,597
The time here's gonna
speed up in ten minutes.

243
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,915
He wants us to log out before it does.

244
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:43,641
All right, then.

245
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:47,291
I wish we could float here
forever, but Alice does need us.

246
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:49,840
Come on, let's go get her. Hang on.

247
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:51,320
We'll be going fast.

248
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:18,840
Amayori and Takiguri, this
is my final order to you.

249
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:22,740
Return to the human empire
and your nests in the west.

250
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:27,320
Amayori, find a husband,
and Takiguri, find a wife.

251
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:30,580
Have many babies and
raise them to be strong.

252
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:33,317
Strong and brave so that one day they may

253
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,988
carry knights as gallantly
as their parents.

254
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:46,060
Go home! Go on!

255
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,740
Ama... Yori?

256
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:57,220
